<title>SPAIN: BCH chairman to propose vice-chairman.</title>
<headline>BCH chairman to propose vice-chairman.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of Spain's Banco Central Hispano will propose at the next board meeting that Angel Corcostegui be named new vice-chairman of the group, replacing the retiring Luis Coronel de Palma, sources at the bank said.</p>
<p>&quot;The proposal is natural, appropriate and useful,&quot; the source told Reuters.</p>
<p>The bank's next board meeting is June 12.</p>
<p>Corcosetegui joined BCH as chief executive in July 1994, having left Banco Bilbao Vizcaya.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
